## Session 15 summary — criteria **not yet met** (marker not written), four root fixes landed

**FIX-H family (the sess14 "tenure-boundary mutex race" — interpretation was inverted):** The r10 one-dirent swallow was not an admit-side race. Node6's `bast_notify` P135 branch misread the TCP **grant-completion window** (receive kworker links the mirror before the blocked acquirer resumes) as an orphan and wire-released node6's *own just-granted tenure* with a valid gen echo → master granted node4 0.7ms later → true double-EX → same-offset dirent adds. Fixed in three layers (GRANTWIN-PARK at queue time, orphan-live abort at the P15 recheck with 4-strike stranded-release escalation, and — the r13 lesson — a **self-demote exemption**, since the P109 EDEADLK recovery is the legitimate resolver entering with the same signature; blocking it wedged the cluster).

**FIX-I (crash_consistency face, fully instrumented):** the test's drop_caches evicts an unpublished child inode on the *creator*; the P78-PUB-SKIP arm then skipped the master claim while nothing made the child's dinode-cluster durable before the dirent went peer-visible — the reader FUA-read prior-mkfs dinodes (UUID verifier reject, proven via objdump offset→line 891) with no BAST and no mirror. The skip arm now forces the child's cluster durable (log force + AIL wait) before the dir handoff returns; fired 126×/run, `settled=1`.

**FIX-J (single_node_paired, 17%→~5%):** ftrace+blktrace proved 211 of 213 log forces came from the throttled every-128th-unlock CIL kick in `mxfs_ag_dlm_unlock` — ~550 extra FLUSH/FUA round-trips per rsync. Gated single-node (multi-node untouched); the bench itself was rebuilt into position-balanced rounds after proving the old protocol was a host-cache coin flip.

**Validation tally:** 8/tcp 17/17 ×7 (r14-r20), 4/tcp ×3, 2/tcp ×4, 1/tcp ×2 clean before the perf work; r21 on the newest build hit a tds 0/8 wedge (ino-158 waiter starvation — r22 running to discriminate FIX-J flap vs known tds long-tail).

**Remaining blockers:** (1) single_node_paired's honest ~5% floor (leads in memory: deferred-unlock kmalloc, heartbeat-read interference, l_logsize); (2) fio_vs_xfs_baseline needs the balanced-rounds treatment; (3) r22 verdict, then streak accumulation on the final build across all four columns.

